From 374052422ff7240ac08d2a3593edda8b2853da06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:07:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Recommendation rank editing and cohort independence

The rank field was pinned to max=1 for Recommendations on legacy v3 state,
because the subsection rank model applied even when no subsections own
ranking. Gate it on persistedState actually carrying recommendationSubsections.

Route the legacy save path through reorderCatalogueCohorts so Main, Half-Cigar
and Taster rank independently. Half-Cigars were consuming positions in the
Recommendation sequence, leaving gaps like 1, 2, 4, 6, 8 after any move.

Write catalogueType from the editor, offer Half-Cigar in the static type
select, drop the dead max=28 attribute, and remove the superseded
reorderCohortOverrides.
